{title: Fullness of Joy}
{subtitle: Psalms 16:11}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 78}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]I have set the LORD always be[Eb]fore me
Because [Gm]he is at my right hand I [Eb]will not be shaken
My [Bb]heart is glad and my [Eb]glory rejoices
My [Cm7]body also rests secure in [Bb]his care
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You make known [Eb]to me the [F]path of life
In [Gm]your presence [Eb]there is fullness [F]of joy
At [Gm]your right hand [Eb]are pleasures [F]forever[Gm]more
[F]I [Eb]hold you [Cm7]close and I am [F]not afraid
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
You will [Bb]not aban[Bb]don my soul to the [Bbmaj7/D]grave
Nor let your faith[Eb]ful one see [Gm]decay
My hope is [Eb]bound to your stead[Bb]fast love
You keep me [Eb]safe through the darkest [Cm7]day
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You make [F]known to me [Bb]the path of life
In [Eb]your presence [F]there is full[Gm]ness of [Eb]joy
At your right [F]hand are plea[Gm]sures forever[Eb]more
I hold [F]you close [Gm]and [F]I [Eb]am not [Cm7]afraid
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
No [F]shadow can take hold [Bb]of [Bbmaj7/A]my [Gm]spirit
Your right hand upholds me [Eb]in every trial
I [Bb]rest secure in the [F]promise you gave
My [Gm]body and soul [Eb]find peace in your arms
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Cm7]You make [Fsus4]known to me the path of [Bb]life
In your [Eb]presence there [F]is fullness of [Gm]joy
At your [Eb]right hand are plea[F]sures fore[Gm]vermore
[Eb]I hold you [F]close and [Gm]I [F]am [Eb]not af[Cm7]raid
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
In your [F]presence there is full[Bb]ness of [Eb]joy
Pleasures [F]forever[Gm]more [Cm7]at your [F]right [Bb]hand
{end_of_verse}

